# Docs freshness

This repo’s product is Markdown under `docs/`. Content changes must land in **every affected file in the same session**. Do not defer documentation.

## Impact map

| If you change | Also update |
| --- | --- |
| Interview / source note | `docs/01-current-process/sources/` **and** `as-is-process.md` / `systems-and-tools.md` when the shared picture changes |
| New or renamed term | `docs/02-requirements/glossary.md`; link the term, do not redefine it elsewhere |
| New capability | Stable ID in `functional-requirements.md` (`FR-00x`) or `non-functional-requirements.md` (`NFR-00x`) |
| Product or architecture choice | New or updated ADR in `docs/06-decisions/` (not only the chat) |
| Phase or agreement status | The matching row in `docs/README.md` (the only status index) and `Last reviewed` on that folder README |
| n8n workflow JSON (later) | Matching sections in `docs/05-design-spec/` and an ADR if the choice is new |

## Do not

- Edit only one file when the same fact is stated elsewhere.
- Put to-be design into `docs/01-current-process/`.
- Invent architecture, functional spec, design spec, or workflows until requirements are agreed.
- Auto-rewrite docs via hooks; ask or patch files explicitly.

## Session close

List which docs you changed and which related docs you **did not** change, with a reason.
